# PyTorch / ML (MBS)

Adapted from awesome-cursorrules PyTorch + scikit-learn and AutoML rules;
chemistry-specific advice stripped. Obey scientific invariants in `AGENTS.md`.

## Architecture

- Keep the **flat DeepRVAT-style max-pooling** baseline available.
- CpG and region aggregation must be **permutation invariant** (use
  `mbs.segment_ops` / shared set encoders).
- Use **LayerNorm or RMSNorm** in the shared encoder; BatchNorm only with an ADR.
- Prefer standard PyTorch ops over mandatory compiled extensions.
- Empty genes → neutral score + false presence mask; missing ≠ low burden.

## Leakage and evaluation

- Sample / study / GSE / donor / platform IDs must **not** enter the shared
  encoder as predictive features.
- Fit normalization and phenotype-derived selection **inside the training fold**.
- No sample scored by a model trained on that sample, donor, replicate, or
  held-out study group (study-grouped cross-fitting).
- Log resolved experiment config into the run artifact directory.

## Training hygiene

- Set seeds; record checkpoint hashes and manifests.
- Use sklearn / torchmetrics for metrics when the training extra is installed;
  keep Lightning optional behind the `training` extra.
- Unit-test reductions and missing-gene behavior on tiny fixtures—not real
  matrices.
